IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23): the shape shared by the three tables of weeks of benefits
-- that have twelve columns of the regional rate of unemployment: Schedule I (by hours of insurable employment),
-- the table that Schedule II, paragraph 18 puts in place of Schedule I (by weeks of insurable employment) and
-- Schedule V (by hours, for seasonal workers). Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here
-- is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- A blank cell of a table is NOTHING: the table gives no number of weeks there, and the Act does not say what that
-- means. The columns are the twelve bands of `Rate band` in the keel (eia-core), in the order of Schedule I.

§ `A row of a table of weeks of benefits`

-- src:3204 | Number of hours of insurable employment in qualifying period | 6% and under | More than 6% but not more than 7% | More than 7% but not more than 8% | More than 8% but not more than 9% | More than 9% but not more than 10% | More than 10% but not more than 11% | More than 11% but not more than 12% | More than 12% but not more than 13% | More than 13% but not more than 14% | More than 14% but not more than 15% | More than 15% but not more than 16% | More than 16%
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule I (src:3204)
DECLARE `ei6 Weeks row` HAS
    `ei6 weeks at 6% and under`                          IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `ei6 weeks at more than 6% but not more than 7%`     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `ei6 weeks at more than 7% but not more than 8%`     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `ei6 weeks at more than 8% but not more than 9%`     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `ei6 weeks at more than 9% but not more than 10%`    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `ei6 weeks at more than 10% but not more than 11%`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `ei6 weeks at more than 11% but not more than 12%`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `ei6 weeks at more than 12% but not more than 13%`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `ei6 weeks at more than 13% but not more than 14%`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `ei6 weeks at more than 14% but not more than 15%`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `ei6 weeks at more than 15% but not more than 16%`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `ei6 weeks at more than 16%`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- The cell of a row in the column of a band; NOTHING for a blank cell.
-- src:3204 | Number of hours of insurable employment in qualifying period | 6% and under | More than 6% but not more than 7% | More than 7% but not more than 8% | More than 8% but not more than 9% | More than 9% but not more than 10% | More than 10% but not more than 11% | More than 11% but not more than 12% | More than 12% but not more than 13% | More than 13% but not more than 14% | More than 14% but not more than 15% | More than 15% but not more than 16% | More than 16%
@ref Employment Insurance Act Schedule I (src:3204)
GIVEN row IS A `ei6 Weeks row`
      band IS A `Rate band`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `ei6 the cell of the row in the column of` IS
    CONSIDER band
    WHEN `6% and under`                          THEN row's `ei6 weeks at 6% and under`
    WHEN `more than 6% but not more than 7%`     THEN row's `ei6 weeks at more than 6% but not more than 7%`
    WHEN `more than 7% but not more than 8%`     THEN row's `ei6 weeks at more than 7% but not more than 8%`
    WHEN `more than 8% but not more than 9%`     THEN row's `ei6 weeks at more than 8% but not more than 9%`
    WHEN `more than 9% but not more than 10%`    THEN row's `ei6 weeks at more than 9% but not more than 10%`
    WHEN `more than 10% but not more than 11%`   THEN row's `ei6 weeks at more than 10% but not more than 11%`
    WHEN `more than 11% but not more than 12%`   THEN row's `ei6 weeks at more than 11% but not more than 12%`
    WHEN `more than 12% but not more than 13%`   THEN row's `ei6 weeks at more than 12% but not more than 13%`
    WHEN `more than 13% but not more than 14%`   THEN row's `ei6 weeks at more than 13% but not more than 14%`
    WHEN `more than 14% but not more than 15%`   THEN row's `ei6 weeks at more than 14% but not more than 15%`
    WHEN `more than 15% but not more than 16%`   THEN row's `ei6 weeks at more than 15% but not more than 16%`
    WHEN `more than 16%`                         THEN row's `ei6 weeks at more than 16%`
